	(gr_text "COLD RAIL (chassis): lip from z = 7.5 mm, body from z = 13.0 mm, top z = 40.0 mm; ceramic pad 0.63 mm, continuous; clips on the plastic body"
		(at 110 197.13 0)
		(layer "Dwgs.User")
		(uuid "a3a423f4-a8e2-47f4-8a56-09992cf15cd5")
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.5 1.5)
				(thickness 0.2)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
	)
	(gr_text "FABRICATION NOTES - PECD P7 REV 1.2 (2026-10-11)\n1. 6 layers, finished thickness 1.6 mm. Outer copper 2 oz, inner 1 oz.\n   F.Cu / prepreg 0.10 / In1 / core 0.46 / In2 / prepreg 0.20 /\n   In3 / core 0.46 / In4 / prepreg 0.10 / B.Cu\n2. Laminate FR-4, CTI >= 600 V (IEC 60112, material group I), Tg >= 150 C.\n3. Dielectric withstand F.Cu (HV_DCP) to In1 (HV_DCN): 2 kV DC, 1 min,\n   every board.\n4. Routed through slots 1.5 mm wide, rounded ends, under the 7 drivers\n   (14.5 mm) and the 4 isolated amplifiers (8.5 mm): see Edge.Cuts.\n5. CONFORMAL COATING both faces over the high-voltage area, with UV tracer;\n   100 % UV inspection. Mask the areas drawn on Cmts.User (connectors,\n   terminals, fixing holes, test points).\n   ALL HV CREEPAGE DISTANCES ASSUME POLLUTION DEGREE 1 FROM THIS COATING.\n6. Depanelise BEFORE coating.\n7. IPC-6012 class 2 minimum. Solder mask both faces, vias tented.\n   White silkscreen top.\n8. Fiducials FID1-FID3 (1 mm, top side) for automatic assembly.\n9. R602-R605 (2 W bleeders, hot spot up to 150 C): body 4 mm above the\n   board, formed leads. Q1xx and Q601: clamp to the cold rail BEFORE\n   soldering (assembly instructions, montaggio.md).\n10. Serial number and date code in the S/N box, every board."
		(at 117 368 0)
		(layer "Dwgs.User")
		(uuid "06fe9531-2462-4e71-9dcc-1a86cae7b08d")
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.6 1.6)
				(thickness 0.2)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
	)
	(gr_text "Cmts.User: COATING KEEP-OUT - mask these areas before conformal coating (fab note 5)"
		(at 380 372 0)
		(layer "Cmts.User")
		(uuid "f7b3eb24-e027-4ebc-aaf0-827e8f479a94")
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.6 1.6)
				(thickness 0.2)
			)
		)
	)
